From 7363fdd03e3e5763b04cbc874680b49ee4d99274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:57:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: cards fade out when closed; the floating "N new"
 label fades in
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next §6.52, second half of its first step (0193 did the fade-in; operator, 2026-11-26:
0204 then 0205). A card closed from Zeo's own controls no longer vanishes: it stays on screen
for CARD_FADE_OUT (150 ms, the fade-in's length, so opening and closing read as one motion
played both ways) while its opacity falls to 0, and only then does its owner run the close it
used to run at once. Under reduce_motion the close is instant, as before.

Where: the /btw card's Close; a tasks-card row's dismiss and "Clear finished". When every row
on show is leaving, the whole card (expanded, pill or bottom bar) fades out with them, so its
frame does not pop away after its rows faded, and the rows do not fade a second time inside it.

Why nothing is copied: a leaving card is still the card -- the /btw card keeps its state with
a `leaving` task; a tasks-card row is still a row (counted, ordered, able to change status),
marked in `leaving_rows` until a detached timer runs the old dismissal. That is also why the
question card is not faded out (operator, 2026-11-26): it closes because the agent resolved the
question, and by then what it showed is gone; keeping a copy for 150 ms is not worth the code.

A leaving card draws under its own id (`<id>-out`), so the fade-out starts fresh rather than
continuing the fade-in's clock. A second Close while the /btw card fades changes nothing; a new
question replaces the leaving card and drops its timer with it.

The floating thread controls are always present, so there is nothing of them to fade; the
"N new" label that appears beside them while auto-scroll is paused fades in like a card. It
goes at once on resume, in the same click that jumps to the end.

Tests: card_fade (fade_out_opacity's ends), thread_view::tests::card_fade_out_tests (the /btw
card stays while leaving and goes after the fade; reduce motion closes at once; a second Close
does not restart the clock; a new question survives the old fade), tasks_card::dismiss_tests
(dismiss and "Clear finished" keep the rows while they fade; reduce motion dismisses at once).
---

